                <pb facs="1006" n="908" sameAs="frus:frus1900/pg908"/>

                <head><hi rendition="#italic">Mr. Hay to Mr. Griscom.</hi></head>
                <opener><seg rendition="#center">[Telegram.—Paraphrase.]</seg></opener>
                <opener><dateline rendition="#float-right"><placeName><hi rendition="#small-caps"
                                >Department of State</hi>,<lb/><hi rendition="#italic"
                                >Washington</hi></placeName>, <date calendar="gregorian"
                            when="1900-05-19"><hi rendition="#italic">May 19,
                        1900</hi></date>.</dateline></opener>
                <p>[Mr. Hay states that the President is confident that His Majesty the Sultan will
                    keep the promise so long ago made to pay indemnity of £20,000, thereby removing
                    all differences between the two Governments and confirming their friendly
                    relations.</p>
                <p>Mr. Griscom is directed to ask that an early day be set for the payment of the
                    sum due, and to once more invite the attention of His Majesty and of the Sublime
                    Porte to the serious nature of the representations made by him on April 24.]</p>
            </div>
        </body>
